  <desc>Write a message to a contact and send it, with files attached,
  through the company's mail account.</desc>
    <credit type="author">
      <name>Reuben Rissler</name>
      <email>pygtk.posting@gmail.com</email>
    </credit>
  </info>

  <title>Send email</title>

  <p>PyGtk Posting sends mail itself, through the account set up in <link
  xref="settings#mail_accounts"/>. The <gui>Send email</gui> window opens
  from:</p>
  <list>
    <item><p>the <gui>Email</gui> button of an <link xref="invoice"/>, with
    an empty message to the customer;</p></item>
    <item><p>posting an invoice with <gui>Email invoice</gui> checked. The
    invoice is attached, and the subject and message are the ones set in
    <link xref="email_message"/>;</p></item>
    <item><p>posting a document with <gui>Email invoice</gui> checked, in
    <link xref="documents_window"/>, with the document attached;</p></item>
    <item><p><gui>Send via email</gui> in <link
    xref="unpaid_invoices#menu"/>, with the summary of the customer's unpaid
    invoices attached.</p></item>
  </list>
  <p>Nothing is sent until you click <gui>Send</gui>, so a message can always
  be read and changed first.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>Choose the <gui>Contact</gui>, or type an address in
    <gui>To</gui>. Only contacts with an email address are listed, and
    choosing one fills in <gui>To</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Type the <gui>Subject</gui> and the message.</p></item>
    <item><p>Under <gui>Attachments</gui>, <gui>Add</gui> attaches files from
    the computer and <gui>Remove</gui> takes the selected one
    off.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click <gui>Send</gui>. It stays greyed out until <gui>To</gui>
    holds an email address.</p></item>
  </steps>

  <p>The line at the bottom says which address the mail goes out from, or
  that no mail account is set up. The message is sent in the background. A
  message then says it was sent and the window closes; if it could not be
  sent, the message says why and the window stays as it was, so you can put
  it right and send again. Attachments that come to more than 20 MB are
  refused before anything is sent.</p>

  <p>A sent message is kept in the database, filed under the contact chosen
  and under the invoice it carried, and can be read in <link
  xref="correspondence"/> on any computer. When the account has an IMAP
  server, a copy is also put in its Sent folder, so it shows in other mail
  programs too.</p>

  <note><p>The password is kept in the login keyring of each computer, not in
  the database, so it has to be set once on every computer that sends mail;
  see <link xref="settings#mail_accounts"/>.</p></note>

</page>
